## The 0.75ct Princess Purchase Checklist

Before buying a 0.75ct princess diamond, confirm each item on this checklist. Every missed check is a potential $200–$600 mistake.

**Diamond checks:**

- Carat weight: 0.72–0.77ct range confirmed (avoid exact 0.75ct threshold premium if budget is tight)
- Cut: GIA Very Good or Excellent — check table 52–58%, depth 64–75% in certificate
- Color: G minimum in white gold or platinum; H acceptable in yellow or rose gold
- Clarity: VS1 confirmed; if VS2, verify GIA plot shows inclusions away from all four corners
- Fluorescence: None or Faint; if Medium, watch HD video for haziness
- GIA report verified: go to gia.edu, enter report number, confirm color/clarity/carat match listing exactly
- HD video reviewed: no visible corner dark spots, no haziness, even brightness across the table

**Setting checks:**

- Setting sized for 5mm princess (0.65–0.85ct range) — not 1ct settings
- 4-corner V-prong confirmed — protects the 90-degree corners from daily chipping
- Metal type matches your color choice (G in white gold; H acceptable in yellow gold)
- Ring size confirmed before ordering (resizing a prong setting is possible but adds cost)

**Purchase checks:**

- Return policy confirmed — Blue Nile offers 30-day returns on diamonds
- GIA certificate will ship with the diamond (not a copy, the physical certificate)
- Total ring budget confirmed: diamond + setting + any engraving + tax + shipping

Farzana keeps a printed version of this checklist at the office. Every buyer who uses it makes fewer post-purchase regret calls.

